# CHANGELOG.md is rendered by git-cliff from commit history (cliff.toml), so it has a
# writer already and nothing here should be its second one. Whatever wrapping the
# template emits is the template's to decide, and a hook that unwrapped the rendered
# output would be overwritten on the next release anyway -- churn in both directions
# for no gain. _typos.toml excludes it as generated content for the same reason.
#
# Nothing else is excluded. The agent-instruction files are deliberately in scope,
# unlike the sibling arrangement in aicadium-lab/exemplary-prs, where they sit outside
# the unwrapper. That exclusion answers a security question this repository does not
# have: there, an automation rewrites prose and then approves its own gated CI runs, so
# it must be unable to touch a file that steers a write-capable agent. Here the hook
# runs at commit time under the hands of whoever is committing, and unwrapping a
# paragraph does not change what it instructs.
CHANGELOG.md
